 "notes": "Spine: need -> PGA-blending hypothesis -> HAP/PLLA base + PGA modification + ratio sweep -> laser printing -> porous blended scaffold -> hydrophilicity -> degradation -> HAP exposure -> apatite formation, against a strength loss -> trade-off -> down-select 3# -> cytocompatibility -> in-vivo repair -> conclusion. Two branches (mechanical b17 vs degradation/bioactivity b11-b16) meet at the trade-off b18. b18->b19 uses motivates from a claim, which the v02 rel definition does not list (proposal filed). The degradation->bioactivity attribution rests on shared ranking across the PGA series (b31 -> b16, correlate_across_series); F6 shows HAP exposure clearly only for 5#, not for 3# (b33 partial). The in-vivo between-group claim has no quantitative support (b40 partial). Omitted: XRD/FTIR/DSC/TGA (F2) and fracture surfaces (F4), not opened; secondary. Cell culture is typed PRP/value biological (in-vitro material response) and bone repair PRF/service_capability (in-vivo application test); see proposal comment on this boundary.",
